Package: sg-mail
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, thunderbird (>= 1:128), sg-davmail (>= 7.0.0), iproute2
Recommends: fonts-inter
Description: SG Mail: mail and calendar for Stained Glass OS (built on Thunderbird)
 SG Mail is Stained Glass OS's mail and calendar program, in a window
 arranged the way many office workers know: a ribbon, the folder pane with
 Favorites, unread counts and Search Folders, the message list grouped by
 date with a Focused Inbox, the reading pane (right, bottom or off), a
 message window, a calendar with Day, Work Week, Week and Month views
 (appointments dragged and resized with the mouse), meeting invitations and
 reminders, and People (contacts and contact groups).
 .
 It is built on Mozilla Thunderbird (unmodified: Stained Glass OS's
 package of Mozilla's official build, or Debian's), which does the work
 underneath: IMAP, POP and SMTP accounts, Exchange and Microsoft 365 mail,
 sign-in to Microsoft (Outlook.com, Microsoft 365) and Google accounts on
 their own login pages, autoconfiguration from the address, the calendar
 (local, CalDAV and Internet calendars), the address book and offline
 storage. SG Mail runs Thunderbird with a profile of its own (sg-mail) and
 makes its main window SG Mail's with a Thunderbird extension.
 .
 Microsoft accounts (Outlook.com, Hotmail, Live, Microsoft 365, Exchange):
 mail, calendars and contacts, read and written, through DavMail (package
 sg-davmail), a gateway SG Mail runs for each account as a user service on
 this computer only; one sign-in to Microsoft, in DavMail's own window.
